Modified 2026-10-24: independent process interface and build; bounded configuration,
preview and recovery; isolated, cancellable fingerprint generation with verified
HTTPS; lifecycle integration and non-destructive handling of conflicting modules.
The in-process injection mechanisms and compatibility rules derive from upstream.
Rule review preserves explicit SDK choices, defaults new Provider compatibility off,
labels Canary heuristics, removes shell evaluation and checks root-runtime evidence.
Build value conversion preserves normalized JSON booleans; generator process groups
are reaped on cancellation, limits, errors and normal completion.
File migration output preserves permissions on existing external directories.
Companion exchanges share a monotonic deadline, invalid UTF-8 is rejected, JNI text
uses standard UTF-8 decoding, and empty stop tokens cannot acknowledge shutdown.
Configuration lock guards explicitly release ownership despite inherited descriptors.
Named configuration snapshots and manual test observations use bounded private
storage. Read-only system/configuration comparison never infers runtime values or
server verdicts. Snapshot selection always produces a fresh application preview.

Modified 2026-10-30: the component is built only into Duck ToolBox's composite
Zygisk payload. Pixel archive downloads use an immutable source revision,
validated identity and partition patch dates, with source metadata in snapshots.
Late OEM property updates require boot completion. Existing CLI, injection,
compatibility, configuration, recovery and diagnostic capabilities are retained.

Modified 2026-10-31: the official Pixel catalog covers 39 phone, foldable and
tablet identities. Official release snapshots bind the complete fingerprint,
incremental version, model, launch API and paired properties. Older source
records remain readable and are identified as incomplete identity records.
Preview requests reject superseded responses while retaining current errors.

Original PIF concepts and mechanisms are credited upstream to kdrag0n's ProtonAOSP
and Universal SafetyNet Fix. Boot scripts derive from Displax's USNF MOD fork.
